WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.275
Not every hunt discovers active attackers, and that is acceptable.

00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:06.030
A successful hunt may uncover malicious activity,

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:10.020
validate that a concern does not currently appear present, identify visibility gaps,

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.290
improve documentation, or refine future hypotheses.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.355
Negative findings can still provide value.

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:17.715
If the hunt was well scoped and the data was strong,

00:00:17.715 --> 00:00:21.295
the team may gain confidence that a specific behavior was not observed during the period

00:00:21.295 --> 00:00:22.090
reviewed.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.465
Findings from hunts can become SIEM correlation rules, EDR detections, playbooks,

00:00:26.465 --> 00:00:29.690
dashboards, enrichment logic, and analyst training materials.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.700
Hunting turns investigative learning into operational improvement.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.100
Over time,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.020
threat hunting strengthens the organization's ability to detect and respond to future

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:37.650
attacks.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:41.255
It helps security teams learn from their own environment instead of relying only on

00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:42.400
generic assumptions.
